	(footprint "Irin:MP1584EN_HW133_2x2Pad_P2.54mm_W10.16mm_L17.78mm"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "043bd47f-f53d-470e-8fe8-1c02cd21f149")
		(at 75.2348 58.4962)
		(descr "MP1584EN adjustable buck module, HW-133A~F clone (silkscreen: 降压模块 / 输入 / 输出). 4 nets, each broken out to 2 redundant through-holes at 0.1in pitch: VIN-/VIN+ on one edge, VOUT-/VOUT+ on the opposite edge, 0.7in apart; the two net pairs on each edge are 0.4in apart center-to-center. CALIPER-MEASURED by owner 2026-10-20 on the physical module: taking one outer hole as 0, the four holes along an edge sit at 0.0 / 0.1 / 0.4 / 0.5 in, and the input edge to output edge spacing is 0.7 in. This CORRECTS Irin:MP1584EN_HW133_2x2Pad_P2.54mm_W7.62mm_L17.78mm, whose across-module spacing was ruler-measured at +/-0.5mm and came out 0.1in too narrow overall (inner holes at +/-0.2in apart instead of 0.3in); the real module does not fit that footprint -- see the rev B erratum in CLAUDE.md. Board outline CALIPER-MEASURED 2026-10-20 at 0.66 x 0.86 in = 16.76 x 21.84 mm (width across the hole rows x length between them), drawn true on F.SilkS; cross-checks against the hole pattern as 0.08 in of board margin on all four sides. Pad numbers match the Irin:BUCK_MODULE schematic symbol (1=IN+ 2=IN- 3=OUT+ 4=OUT-). Rectangular pads mark the '+' nets (IN+, OUT+), matching the square pads printed on the real board next to its own '+' silkscreen -- also serves as the footprint's pin-1 indicator.")
		(tags "MP1584EN HW-133 buck module perfboard")
